23:     """
24:     Move each non-bar foreground pixel one row downward, and splash diagonal rays upward when it lands directly above the bar.
25: 
26:     Input structure
27:     - The background is the dominant color.
28:     - One foreground color forms a single full-width horizontal bar.
29:     - The only other foreground color appears as isolated moving pixels off the bar.
30: 
31:     Rule
32:     - Clear the moving pixels from their original locations and paint each one at the same column one row lower.
33:     - If a moved pixel lands immediately above the horizontal bar, also paint both upward diagonals from that landing pixel until they leave the grid.
34:     - The full-width bar and all background cells outside those shifted/splashed paths remain unchanged.
35: 
36:     Key insight
37:     - The bar is a trigger line: pixels always shift down one step, but only pixels that become adjacent to the bar emit the diagonal splash.
38:     """
39:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
40:     assert g.ndim == 2, "expected a 2D grid"
